  "response": "두 상황에서 공통적으로 보이는 걸 스스로 발견하신 거네요. 상대가 이미 사과를 했거나 실수가 사소한 것이었는데도, 그 이상으로 밀어붙인 뒤 관계가 상하고, 그 뒤에 '이게 정말 원칙인가' 하고 스스로에게 되묻는 패턴이요.\n\n'원칙인지, 다른 건지 모르겠다'는 그 경계가 흐려진 느낌이 꽤 불편하셨을 것 같습니다. 그 '다른 것'이라는 게 혹시 어떤 느낌으로 다가올 때가 있는지, 떠올려보실 수 있을까요?",
  "reasoning": "The client is sharing two recent incidents where they felt their responses were disproportionate - the strict punishment of their son (phone confiscation for a month after he already apologized, despite husband suggesting to give a chance) and the public demand for a corrective document from a colleague who made a minor mistake. \n\nThe client's core question is self-reflective: \"Why have I become so sharp? Is this principle or something else?\"\n\nThis is a rich moment. The client is already doing some self-examination - they're not asking for validation, they're genuinely confused about their own behavior. They're distinguishing between \"principle\" and \"something else\" - suggesting they suspect there might be an emotional driver beyond their stated values.\n\nWhat would be helpful here?\n- Not rushing to diagnose or label what's going on\n- Not immediately suggesting \"maybe you're stressed\" or \"maybe you need to relax\"\n- Honoring the self-awareness they're already showing\n- Perhaps gently exploring what \"principle\" means to them, or what the \"something else\" might be\n- I could reflect back the pattern they've noticed (both situations involve a transgression → disproportionate response → relationship damage)\n- Or I could explore what the \"something else\" might feel like to them\n- Or I could ask about what's changed - what's different now vs. \"before\" when they were also principled but perhaps not this sharp\n\nI think the most helpful response would be to:\n1. Acknowledge the self-awareness and the discomfort of that self-questioning\n2. Gently reflect the pattern they've identified\n3. Invite exploration of what the \"something else\" might be - what it feels like, what it might be protecting, or what's changed\n\nI want to avoid being too interpretive or jumping to conclusions. I'll reflect and open a door.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n\"두 상황에서 공통적으로 보이는 패턴을 스스로 발견하신 거네요. 원칙을 지키는 것과, 그 원칙이 실제로는 다른 감정을 대신 말하고 있는 것 사이의 경계가 흐려진 걸 느끼시는 것 같습니다. '다른 건지 모르겠다'는 말씀에서, 그 '다른 것'이 무엇일지 감이 오시는 부분이 있을까요?\"\n\nHmm, this is decent but maybe I can be a bit more grounded. Let me think about what feels most natural and helpful.\n\nActually, I think reflecting the pattern and then gently opening toward what the \"something else\" might be is the right move. The client is already halfway there - they're asking the right question. My job is to help them go a bit further without pushing them.\n",
